CM 8-turn axial-mode helix for 435 MHz over a ground reflector (perfect ground here)
CM GH builds the helix along +Z from the origin; GM lifts it by 'gap'; tag 2 is the feed wire.
CM The helix is about 220 ohm, so a 1:4 transformer from a separate source wire (tag 3) matches 50 ohm.
CE
SY f=435, lam=299.79/f, D=lam/pi, S=0.25*lam, N=8, r=1.5mm, gap=0.03
GH 1 128 S N*S D/2 D/2 D/2 D/2 r
GM 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 gap 1
GW 2 2 D/2 0 0 D/2 0 gap r
GW 3 1 1 1 0.2 1 1 0.21 1mm ' source wire for transformer
GE 1
GN 1
EX 0 3 1 0 1 0
NT 3 1 2 1 4000 0 -2000 0 1000 0 ' xfmr 1:4
FR 0 36 0 0 400 2
EN
